---
description: One card, one scope. The rule that makes a wave of agents safe to merge in any order.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Scope

Every card in `tasks/` declares the paths it may touch. `task-lint` compares
the working diff to the card's `scope` and fails on anything outside it.

This is what makes a whole wave of agents safe to merge in any order: within
a wave, scopes are disjoint by construction, so there is nothing to conflict
over.

- Touching a file outside your card's scope is a **failed card**, even when
  the change is correct and the tests pass.
- If working your card requires a change outside its scope, **stop** and say
  so in the PR body. That is a finding, not a failure.
- Do not fix the neighbouring bug. Do not tidy the adjacent file. Do not
  start the next card because it is obvious.

`package.json` is the one deliberately shared path — H005 appends
`content-lint` to the `law` line. `task-lint` exempts it and nothing else.
